@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# QB_HEAD: the passer's head turns at the shared rate (attempt 1, off)
+
+Integration's go, 2026-11-16 (Defense's zone trace: qb.ts set `a.head` to his gaze point every tick, so his head
+jumped between reads in a tick and zone defenders who lean on his eyes stepped with it, 30% of their reversals). The
+shared head (src/sim/head.ts, HEAD, off) skipped the passer by design ("until the QB lane moves it to want").
+
+## What it does
+
+- His head turns toward the point he wants to look at by head.ts's one turn (`turnHead`, extracted from `stepHeads`,
+  which now calls it: HEAD on is unchanged): 6 rad/s within the shared neck range off his body facing, over the
+  shoulder for a target behind. The same function whether HEAD is on or off.
+- His picture is taken along where his head points, at the gaze's range (`mind.observe`, `receiverLook`); his clear
+  look (`inClearLook`) is about his head.
+- Defenders read `a.head` as before; it now moves at the rate.
+
+## Timings calibrated on the instant head (Integration's condition 2)
+
+| timing | what it is | under QB_HEAD |
+|---|---|---|
+| HEAD_RATE 400 deg/s in the hot look (`hotLook`'s `turn`) | a timed head turn before his eyes are on the hot target | **double count, removed**: his eyes are on the man once his head points within 0.15 rad of him (chosen), then the glance |
+| the glance (0.15 + 0.2 (1 - dm) + 0.1 (1 - aw)) | the time to take a man in once his eyes are there | unaffected (it starts on arrival now) |
+| read dwell (`readDwell`, `readStart`) and bit 1's beats (`beatDue`, eyes leave a stride before the step) | when he moves off a read, counted from the read change | needs re-reading: part of the dwell is now spent turning (read change to eyes on the read p90 0.30 -> 0.45 s); not charged twice, so unchanged here |
+| QB_LOOKOFF (0.25-0.35 s on the decoy) | a fixed hold of his eyes on the decoy side | needs re-reading: the head's travel to the decoy and back eats into it; what defenders see of it is now physical |
+| the key read's cueBy | the key read at the plan's cue, from his memory pictures | needs re-reading: how fresh the key man's picture is depends on where his head has been |
+| QB_EYES' eyesOnAt / gate | when his eyes are taken to be on a read | needs re-reading (measured from the gaze change, not the arrival); unchanged here |
+
+## Gate (staged)
+
+- Head rate (scripts/diag/eyes/head-rate.ts, 6 concepts x 4 coverages x 2 rosters x 2 seeds): off p50 4, p95 432,
+  p99 1662, max 3313 deg/s; on p50 6, p95 344, max 344 (none over the rate).
+- Read change to his eyes on the new read: p50 0.05 / 0.05 s, p90 0.30 -> 0.45 s.
+- Paired dropbacks (drop-staged.ts, the 16 staged concepts, 3072 plays, engine defaults): sacks 5.6 -> 5.9%,
+  interceptions 47 -> 39, completions 1946 -> 1936, yd 8.54 -> 8.48, time to throw mean 3.14 -> 3.15 s (median 3.05 /
+  3.05). The cost is where his eyes swing across the field: verts_hitch sacks 11 -> 18 (throw 3.59 -> 3.69 s),
+  four_verts completions 68 -> 61.
+- Defenders' eyes-read timing: Defense's ZONE_HOLD bit 32 (lean on the seen head line) to be read with it.
+
+## Follow-up list (Integration, 2026-11-16)
+
+To be re-read on the card after QB_HEAD's, not changed now: read dwell and bit 1's beats; QB_LOOKOFF's hold; the key
+read's cueBy; QB_EYES' eyesOnAt. The 0.15 rad "eyes on" in the hot look is chosen. Card arms: QB_HEAD alone; with
+ZONE_HOLD=114 (Defense); with bit 2. Patch: docs/reviews/patches/engine71-footwork/9-qb-head-after-6-8.patch, against
+rules/key-sits ad225b1a + Flex's pocket-drop + patches 6, 7, 8 (FLAGS hand-merged).
